            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htSlides\"><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">1 / 2</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"z0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('z0', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Gourd in a Zimbabwean cooking pot. Photo used with permission from Dr. Zvakanyorwa Wilbert Sadomba (<htcite0>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Continuity - When we look around us and at ourselves, we don't see gaps everywhere. In this text, we begin to see how to connect things. (<htcite1>)</li><li>Cooking - The preparation of food is often remembered for adding quantities, but there is also another side to it. (<htcite2>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">2 / 2</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgShona1\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgShona1', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Diagram of the Shona kitchen. Photo used with permission from Dr. Zvakanyorwa Wilbert Sadomba (<htcite3>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Cooking with numbers - Generally, recipes contain natural numbers. However, the final result is quite real. (<htcite4>)</li></ul></div></div><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left htSlidePrev\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(-1);\"></i><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right htSlideNext\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(1);\"></i></div></p>",
